@node Installation and Requirements
@chapter Installation and Requirements
@cindex installation
@cindex requirements

This chapter lists what @code{beads.el} needs and how to install and set
it up.  Once it is installed, continue with @ref{Getting Started}.

@menu
* Requirements::
* Installing from MELPA::
* Installing from Source::
* Initial Setup::
@end menu

@node Requirements
@section Requirements
@cindex requirements

@itemize @bullet
@item
Emacs 29.1 or newer.
@item
The @command{bd} executable on @var{PATH}.
@item
The MELPA libraries @code{transient} (0.10.1+) and @code{vui} (1.0.0+).
@item
@command{dolt} and @command{graphviz} for the full feature set and the
complete test suite.
@end itemize

@node Installing from MELPA
@section Installing from MELPA
@cindex MELPA

The package is published on MELPA:

@lisp
(use-package beads
  :ensure t)
@end lisp

@node Installing from Source
@section Installing from Source
@cindex installing from source

Clone the repository and add its @file{lisp/} directory to your load
path:

@lisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "/path/to/beads.el/lisp")
(require 'beads)
@end lisp

@node Initial Setup
@section Initial Setup
@cindex initial setup
@cindex @command{bd} init

Initialize a Beads store in a project directory:

@example
cd /path/to/project
bd init
@end example

Then open the board in Emacs with @kbd{M-x beads}.  @code{beads.el}
finds the store from the buffer's @code{default-directory}; act on a
different project with the @code{:directory} argument
(@pxref{Store Scoping}).
